 the stage where it  can be detected by other civilizations  this could be because there is some  deadly factor about the universe that we  do not know or understand  which is ultimately lethal to life  before it can become a galactic faring  civilization  or it could be because advanced  civilizations are ultimately  self-destructive  humanity seems to have a bright future  i.e  a non-trivial chance of expanding to  fill the universe with lasting life but  the fact that space nearest seems dead  now  tells us that any given piece of dead  matter faces an  astronomically low chance of beginning  such a future  there thus exist a great filter between  death and  expanding lasting life and humanity  faces the ominous question  how far along this filter are we robin  hansen the great filter  are we almost past it 1998  in previous videos we have discussed the  existence of aliens in the dune universe  officially there are no aliens at all in  the series  although humankind has the ability to  fold space  traveling nearly instantaneously between  worlds  alien life has never been found on other  planets  the only exception is potentially the  sand worms  though it is not explicitly stated that  they were  forms of alien life they could have for  instance been the result of genetic  manipulation of animals originating from  old earth  now frank herbert's decision not to  include aliens in the dune saga  is widely accepted to be intentional he  wanted his story to focus on humanity  entirely but this does not prevent us  from discussing dune  and the context of the fermi paradox  we've also previously discussed krelizek  in previous videos on this channel  kralozak also known as the typhoon  struggle  is a friend myth about a great testing  event for humanity in the future  i think it seems likely that the typhoon  struggle relates to the coming of the  enemy  god emperor lato ii saw coming for  humanity and its future  his entire 4000 year reign was meant to  prepare humanity for the struggle  against that enemy  and ensure their indefinite survival  when considering the idea of this great  enemy i can't help but be reminded of  the concept of the great filter  many have guessed at what lato's great  enemy could potentially be  but it seems clear to me that it is of  human origin  as i said dune is a human story  in the book god emperor of dune later  the second mentions seeking machines  capable of hunting down and killing all  humans who did not have the ability to  hide from prescient sight  seeking machines is almost certainly a  reference to hunter seeker devices  only more advanced science fiction  including dune often warns about the  reckless pursuit of technology  if humankind likely the ixians managed  to create  a killing device with prescient  capabilities  and set it loose upon humanity it is  likely that it would eventually move  beyond their control  perhaps the dune saga is suggesting that  the great filter  is caused by the fact that  technologically advanced species  ultimately created technologies that  were destructive to themselves  when a species grows large enough it  eventually begins to act as a super  organism  no individual within that organism can  control the whole  once the magic and horror of technology  is unleashed  it cannot be contained again the army  fostered technology because the power of  machines appeared so obvious to the  short-sighted  that lasegun is no more than a machine  but all machines fail or are superseded  still the army worships at the shrine of  such things  both fascinated and fearful look at how  people fear the ixians  in its guts the army knows it is the  sorcerer's apprentice  it unleashes technology and never again  can the magic be stuffed back into the  bottle  but even that wouldn't really explain  the lack of any life whatsoever on any  of the worlds explored in the dune saga  but perhaps this fact reflects the  actual size of the universe  perhaps the demon universe 